(1068570, 126979, 13749, '<td valign="top">great shot, but since i''m assuming that this is set-up, i would''ve preferred a different set of shoes and socks - they tend to detract from the solemn/grimey(?) theme that is going on here.</td>', 'great shot, but since i''m assuming that this is set-up, i would''ve preferred a different set of shoes and socks - they tend to detract from the solemn/grimey(?) theme that is going on here.', '2004-12-19 01:32:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1068572, 128000, 13749, '<td valign="top">not sure if i like the harsh pink background, especially since it is evident that it has caused some color to flower over the hood of the car (not reflected, but looks more like scattered pink).  may sound too ho-hum, but i think a white background would''ve worked better here</td>', 'not sure if i like the harsh pink background, especially since it is evident that it has caused some color to flower over the hood of the car (not reflected, but looks more like scattered pink).  may sound too ho-hum, but i think a white background would''ve worked better here', '2004-12-19 01:33:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1068574, 127813, 13749, '<td valign="top">love your choice of frame and subjects.  took me a second to realize that it was broken glass - but, this is one of my favorites in the challenge.  i wonder perhaps how a shallow DOF with the windshield in focus might have looked.  10.</td>', 'love your choice of frame and subjects.  took me a second to realize that it was broken glass - but, this is one of my favorites in the challenge.  i wonder perhaps how a shallow DOF with the windshield in focus might have looked.  10.', '2004-12-19 01:35:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1068575, 127432, 13749, '<td valign="top">maybe i''m mistaken, but it looks like there is some extra broken glass in the shot that didn''t come from the bulb - kind of confuses me as to how it got there (of course, you put it there -but you know what i mean).  perhaps deeper depth-of-focus would be good here, as the only thing that really seems to be in focus is the left foreground piece of the bulb.</td>', 'maybe i''m mistaken, but it looks like there is some extra broken glass in the shot that didn''t come from the bulb - kind of confuses me as to how it got there (of course, you put it there -but you know what i mean).  perhaps deeper depth-of-focus would be good here, as the only thing that really seems to be in focus is the left foreground piece of the bulb.', '2004-12-19 01:37:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1068577, 126334, 13749, '<td valign="top">intense.  normally i would say it looks overexposed, has a color cast, and some vignetting - but they all seem to give it a unique look that is appealing this time around.</td>', 'intense.  normally i would say it looks overexposed, has a color cast, and some vignetting - but they all seem to give it a unique look that is appealing this time around.', '2004-12-19 01:38:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1068579, 127506, 13749, '<td valign="top">i know a faster shutter speed was required to freeze motion, but can''t find a place that''s in focus for me to look at.  this is also one that perhaps a uniform black background isn''t beneficial, since it now just looks like the glass is exploding instead of ''seeing'' the interesting impact as it hits some kind of tangible surface</td>', 'i know a faster shutter speed was required to freeze motion, but can''t find a place that''s in focus for me to look at.  this is also one that perhaps a uniform black background isn''t beneficial, since it now just looks like the glass is exploding instead of ''seeing'' the interesting impact as it hits some kind of tangible surface', '2004-12-19 01:40:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1068580, 127984, 13749, '<td valign="top">i like your choice of alignment.  so far it''s the only ''orderly'' broken glass that i''ve seen in the challenge, which makes it interesting.  choice of a cool-toned background color also provides the ''calm'' environment that helps fit with this orderly arrangement.  well done.</td>', 'i like your choice of alignment.  so far it''s the only ''orderly'' broken glass that i''ve seen in the challenge, which makes it interesting.  choice of a cool-toned background color also provides the ''calm'' environment that helps fit with this orderly arrangement.  well done.', '2004-12-19 01:42:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1068582, 127560, 13749, '<td valign="top">haha - interesting.  maybe a rearrangement of the middle cookie (it seems to remove some attention away from the fortune) combined with slightly less DOF.</td>', 'haha - interesting.  maybe a rearrangement of the middle cookie (it seems to remove some attention away from the fortune) combined with slightly less DOF.', '2004-12-19 01:43:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1068584, 127744, 13749, '<td valign="top">interesting, but purple hue of the sky gives it a look that i''m not sure is best for this image.  perhaps a darker/rustier looking hue/saturation modification for the truck would work wonders.</td>', 'interesting, but purple hue of the sky gives it a look that i''m not sure is best for this image.  perhaps a darker/rustier looking hue/saturation modification for the truck would work wonders.', '2004-12-19 01:44:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1068585, 127442, 13749, '<td valign="top">um.<br/> <br/>okay, i''m guessing there''s some elaborate sort of setup here, otherwise you probably wasted a lot of eggs!   if you want to use sidelighting in this manner, i''d prefer to see it illuminating the side that the bullet is emerging from, as i''m not sure that its current arrangement contributes much.<br/> <br/>p.s. good idea.</td>', 'um. okay, i''m guessing there''s some elaborate sort of setup here, otherwise you probably wasted a lot of eggs!   if you want to use sidelighting in this manner, i''d prefer to see it illuminating the side that the bullet is emerging from, as i''m not sure that its current arrangement contributes much. p.s. good idea.', '2004-12-19 01:46:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1068586, 127997, 13749, '<td valign="top">oh no - hate it when that happens.  perhaps less lighting on the hand would help improve this interesting shot... or if you''re feeling daring, i have an inkling that a very shallow DOF that only keeps the cork in focus would work quite well here (if that''s possible - i realize everything is at a relatively equal distance from the camera)</td>', 'oh no - hate it when that happens.  perhaps less lighting on the hand would help improve this interesting shot... or if you''re feeling daring, i have an inkling that a very shallow DOF that only keeps the cork in focus would work quite well here (if that''s possible - i realize everything is at a relatively equal distance from the camera)', '2004-12-19 01:49:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1068587, 127356, 13749, '<td valign="top">interesting.  i feel the gradation to black is a little too sudden for my tastes, but this is a good idea and an interesting twist on this common subject.</td>', 'interesting.  i feel the gradation to black is a little too sudden for my tastes, but this is a good idea and an interesting twist on this common subject.', '2004-12-19 01:49:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(1068590, 127504, 13749, '<td valign="top">great idea, with some humor included as well.  two suggestions: one, the two shadows is semi-distracting (just for normal situation/reality purposes) - it does happen, but in this case it just reminds me that it''s a setup shot with (i''m guessing) two lights shining on the pencil.  two, get a newer and smoother textured pencil (and maybe sharpen it as well) - texture is sometimes interesting, but a smooth texture would appeal more to me here.  still, a good shot and worthy of a solid score.</td>', 'great idea, with some humor included as well.  two suggestions: one, the two shadows is semi-distracting (just for normal situation/reality purposes) - it does happen, but in this case it just reminds me that it''s a setup shot with (i''m guessing) two lights shining on the pencil.  two, get a newer and smoother textured pencil (and maybe sharpen it as well) - texture is sometimes interesting, but a smooth texture would appeal more to me here.  still, a good shot and worthy of a solid score.', '2004-12-19 01:54:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1068592, 126802, 13749, '<td valign="top">interesting use of this common subject - if you want to use one light source however, i would prefer to have it illuminating the broken side of the egg, its insides, and the pan rather than the untouched/unbroken side.  possibly including the entire egg would be beneficial as well.</td>', 'interesting use of this common subject - if you want to use one light source however, i would prefer to have it illuminating the broken side of the egg, its insides, and the pan rather than the untouched/unbroken side.  possibly including the entire egg would be beneficial as well.', '2004-12-19 01:55:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1068594, 127958, 13749, '<td valign="top">interesting.  not sure i like the negative space at the top, or the close cut to the tail at the bottom - perhaps a different angle.  texture is great, and so is the contrast.</td>', 'interesting.  not sure i like the negative space at the top, or the close cut to the tail at the bottom - perhaps a different angle.  texture is great, and so is the contrast.', '2004-12-19 01:57:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1068596, 127897, 13749, '<td valign="top">not sure, but i''m guessing the broken part of the image here is what looks like either a strangely shaped fallen tree or (much more likely) an abandoned car.  however, not sure most people will catch this - a different angle might have emphasized this aspect of the photo better.  good colors/contrast however.</td>', 'not sure, but i''m guessing the broken part of the image here is what looks like either a strangely shaped fallen tree or (much more likely) an abandoned car.  however, not sure most people will catch this - a different angle might have emphasized this aspect of the photo better.  good colors/contrast however.', '2004-12-19 01:59:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1068598, 127475, 13749, '<td valign="top">interesting idea.  have seen another broken pencil so far, but not quite as many as i expected.  broken pencil just seems thrown in there, and not necessarily the main focus/theme of the image.  perhaps would''ve rotated the pencil to avoid displaying the USA (2) symbols.</td>', 'interesting idea.  have seen another broken pencil so far, but not quite as many as i expected.  broken pencil just seems thrown in there, and not necessarily the main focus/theme of the image.  perhaps would''ve rotated the pencil to avoid displaying the USA (2) symbols.', '2004-12-19 02:01:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1068599, 127816, 13749, '<td valign="top">hmm.. looks maybe foggy or something - i really like the angle and exposure you''ve chosen - i think the silhouette serves this picture well.  the sky does seem a bit dull, but not sure how to correct that (i''m guessing it was overcast?  not sure)</td>', 'hmm.. looks maybe foggy or something - i really like the angle and exposure you''ve chosen - i think the silhouette serves this picture well.  the sky does seem a bit dull, but not sure how to correct that (i''m guessing it was overcast?  not sure)', '2004-12-19 02:02:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1068602, 126448, 13749, '<td valign="top">haha - excellent.  perhaps more DOF would be in order, since i can''t tell an advantage to just focusing on the first shell, nor a disadvantage if you had included the second one.  maybe slightly more lighting, since the corners seem a bit dark</td>', 'haha - excellent.  perhaps more DOF would be in order, since i can''t tell an advantage to just focusing on the first shell, nor a disadvantage if you had included the second one.  maybe slightly more lighting, since the corners seem a bit dark', '2004-12-19 02:04:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1068605, 127648, 13749, '<td valign="top">seems like a quite unnatural arrangement for a broken bottle.  perhaps a more scattered spread of the glass and, i hate to say it, more wine on the ground (well, let''s not get hasty here!  maybe more cranberry juice.  or $2 charles shaw from trader joes ;).)</td>', 'seems like a quite unnatural arrangement for a broken bottle.  perhaps a more scattered spread of the glass and, i hate to say it, more wine on the ground (well, let''s not get hasty here!  maybe more cranberry juice.  or $2 charles shaw from trader joes ;).)', '2004-12-19 02:05:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(1068608, 127657, 13749, '<td valign="top">good idea, but would''ve liked it better if the bones were a bit ''cleaner'' (ie: entirely bare of everything), as unrealistic as it may seem or look.  also, i think i might''ve liked a white background better here (not sure why)</td>', 'good idea, but would''ve liked it better if the bones were a bit ''cleaner'' (ie: entirely bare of everything), as unrealistic as it may seem or look.  also, i think i might''ve liked a white background better here (not sure why)', '2004-12-19 02:07:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1068609, 127649, 13749, '<td valign="top">interesting interpretation, but not sure what relevance the flys serve.  if you could somehow have managed to get only the R in focus (and eliminated the flys and gradient to brown from top to bottom), this could be great!</td>', 'interesting interpretation, but not sure what relevance the flys serve.  if you could somehow have managed to get only the R in focus (and eliminated the flys and gradient to brown from top to bottom), this could be great!', '2004-12-19 02:08:40.000000', NULL, 1),
