(1070463, 127841, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by strags:</b></div><hr/><i> A good take on the challenge, but a little "snapshot"-ish. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Not a little, but a lot -- still a "photojournalistic snapshot" of something in the process of being broken.<br/> <br/>I should have tried it in B&amp;W to deal with the color-cast issues; I''m not good at color adjustment anyway, and it was shot in very dim light from a variety of industrial and decorative sources. I''m surprised I got it as in-focus as it is.</td>', 'Originally posted by strags: A good take on the challenge, but a little "snapshot"-ish.  Not a little, but a lot -- still a "photojournalistic snapshot" of something in the process of being broken. I should have tried it in B&W to deal with the color-cast issues; I''m not good at color adjustment anyway, and it was shot in very dim light from a variety of industrial and decorative sources. I''m surprised I got it as in-focus as it is.', '2004-12-20 11:09:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(1070496, 127664, 714, '<td valign="top">This shot would have been kewl without the man too.  Fabulious! Congrats</td>', 'This shot would have been kewl without the man too.  Fabulious! Congrats', '2004-12-20 11:31:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(1070503, 127346, 25754, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the blue Dan!</td>', 'Congrats on the blue Dan!', '2004-12-20 11:35:45.000000', NULL, 0),
